  "passage": "A village turned off some streetlights near a river path for one month to help fireflies return. Safety lights remained at important corners, but bright lights near the water were reduced.\nSome residents worried the path would feel unsafe. Volunteers guided evening walks and explained firefly life cycles.\nWhen fireflies appeared, people were amazed.\nThe village learned that darkness is not always a problem. In the right place, managed carefully, it can be habitat.\nThe firefly path taught residents to think differently about light. Human comfort matters, but so do the needs of small lives that disappear when nights become too bright.",
